Upstream-Name: wopr
Upstream-Contact: https://github.com/GhostofGoes/WOPR/issues
Source: https://github.com/GhostofGoes/WOPR
Disclaimer: wopr is a fan-made homage to the 1983 film WarGames. It quotes short
 passages of the text that the film shows on the WOPR computer's terminal.
 Those quotations remain the property of their copyright holders and are not
 licensed under the Expat (MIT) licence; the files that hold them are listed
 below with a comment that says so. This project is not affiliated with,
 endorsed by, or sponsored by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer, United Artists, or anyone
 involved in making the film. NOTICE.md says more; the package installs it
 beside this file.
Comment: Generated by "go run ./internal/tools/notices" from LICENSE, NOTICE.md,
 the provenance tags in the source and the Go modules' licences; do not edit
 it by hand. The program is statically linked. Each Files paragraph whose
 pattern starts with a Go module path (std is the Go standard library and
 runtime) covers the code linked in from that module. "wopr --licenses"
 prints those licences exactly as each module ships them.

